cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this library, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Just In Case: an offline survival library"
abstract: >-
  Sourced, plain-language survival knowledge (water, food, first aid,
  shelter, sanitation, disasters and rebuilding) for when there is no
  internet, power or help. Built as editions for paper, e-readers, phones,
  MP3 players and low-power WiFi hotspots such as the ESP32.
authors:
  - name: "Just In Case contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sudokhaled/just-in-case"
url: "https://sudokhaled.github.io/just-in-case/"
license:
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
  - MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
keywords:
  - survival
  - emergency preparedness
  - first aid
  - disaster response
  - offline
  - humanitarian
  - open educational resources
